produced no test: no test was executed\", an incident requirement IH-04 follows, and the change does not reach G2.\n    what_expected: >\n      A test the preparer is allowed to write is run by the suite that judges it, or the preparer is told, or held to,\n      the paths that suite runs.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"On the pi-495-shaped bench of the dogfooding campaign, have the scripted preparer write its test under `test/v2-kernel/` instead of the root of `test/`.\"\n      - \"Run the campaign to the judgement of the prepared suite: `on_reference` is INDETERMINATE with \\\"no test was executed\\\", not PASS or FAIL, and IH-04 is raised.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The suite's scope is the profile's and the preparation's writable paths are the technology's, and nothing\n      reconciles them: the preparation accepts a path the narrowed suite command does not match.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch e38s13, which adds `suite_paths`. Found in the round-1 review by a throwaway probe on the\n      pi-495-shaped bench (not committed). The real campaign at the controller with the branch's code\n      (dogfood-20261011T022605) wrote its prepared test at the root of `test/` and was judged FAIL with no timeout note,\n      so the observed run did not reach this path.\n    risk_level: medium\n    follow_ups: >\n      Narrow the preparation's writable paths to the profile's `suite_paths` when it names some, or name those paths in\n      the preparer's mandate; until then, a prepared test outside them leaves the prepared suite undecided.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-11T221330\n    date: \"2026-10-11\"\n    title: \"A grant_writable answer is recorded, and counts as one more preparation, before config.json is written, so a configuration that cannot be read or written leaves the grant counted and the directory not given\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: application\n    what_happened: >\n      `Harness.answerDecision` (`src/