, three preparations ran, G2 passed and the frozen unit control carried no\n      writable path.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Write the configuration before committing the answer and refuse the answer with a DomainError when the write\n      fails, or record the failure and re-ask; until then, a failed grant shows as an exception and the owner edits\n      config.json by hand.\n    status: open\n0e36ee97 docs: the registry no longer records defects of the reading of kernel refusals, that reading being gone\nf1c8b9ff docs: the registry records only the refusal count of ten or more as unheld, a refused path holding a line terminator being read whole\nd61e0ecc docs: the registry records that the reading of kernel refusals tells the kernel apart only by the image name a confined process can take, and that no test holds a refusal count of ten or more nor a path holding a line terminator","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"315b9c12-134d-4ae6-8a5d-6e74be2d6773","uuid":"6f8bd643-11cc-498f-9d10-d94d8217f309","timestamp":"2026-10-12T10:13:06.233Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bugs:\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-09-27T170100\n    date: \"2026-09-27\"\n    title: \"G1 accepts a mandatory requirement's satisfied_by_reference claim without evidence, before G2/G5 are known to catch a false one\"\n    severity: medium\n    priority: p2\n    scope: domain\n    what_happened: >\n      A material answer bound to a mandatory requirement passes G1 (`gateG1`, `src/domain/change/decide.ts`)\n      as soon as the requirement is named, is mandatory, and the binding is observable — G1 never reads\n      `satisfied_by_reference`. A specification report can mark a brand-new, never-implemented\n      requirement `satisfied_by_reference: true` (a claim reserved for behaviour the project already\n      honours, per the `specify` role's own instructions) and still clear G1 unchallenged.\n    what_expected: >\n      A material answer resolved only by a false `sati