.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      The survey checks the kind of an entry and then opens it by path, two calls a concurrent writer may separate,\n      and only the Seatbelt profile keeps the run's processes from changing the copy afterwards.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch e40s03, which adds the survey. Found in the round-1 review by reading and by probes\n      under Seatbelt, where the swap is refused; the race was not run under bubblewrap, so no bypass is demonstrated.\n      Reading the bwrap arguments confirms they carry no `--unshare-pid` and that `unremovable_paths` is read only by\n      the Seatbelt backend.\n    risk_level: medium\n    follow_ups: >\n      Run the race under bwrap in the Linux VM; if it holds, add `--unshare-pid` to the bwrap arguments so no process of\n      the run outlives it, or walk the copy through directory descriptors opened with O_NOFOLLOW.\n    status: open\nEOF\nnode -e 'const y=require(\"/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/node_modules/yaml\");' 2>/dev/null; ls node_modules/yaml >/dev/null 2>&1 && node -e 'const y=require(\"yaml\");const d=y.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(\"specs/bugs/registry.yaml\",\"utf8\"));console.log(d.bugs.length, d.bugs.at(-1).bug_id)'","description":"Append registry entries and parse YAML"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_0198yMpfFBUfidM77HNscXd5":{"cwd":"/Users/jeanjerome/Projets/495-pi-package"}}}
